Product Overview ‹#› Compared with Traditional Formwork Prints wall shape directly Eliminates build-strip-repair-clean cycle Can save around 311 labor hours per home Cuts total production costs by ~ 47%-50% How We Differentiate Cuts labor and material costs to help make homes more affordable. Compared with Other Concrete Printers Uses common local concrete, not mortar mix External gate controls flow at the nozzle Avoids high cost mortar dependence Cuts material costs by ~ 60%-65% [Speaker Notes] Atkins

Development Stage and Timeline ‹#› Development Stage and Timeline TRL 6 - 7 MVP: Customer Requirements: Rapid deployment Reduced labor requirements Structural reliability Use locally sourced materials in application environment [Speaker Notes] Will The TRL is 6-7 and there is an MVP for this 3D printer, but as we have not done We want it to stay quick and easy: so moving needs to be easy and using the thing should be easy. Lower for cheaper to build and transport, Cumbersome
**bc this is what customers want, this is why we’re devleopin this way

