Slide 12 ‹#› IP U.S. Patent 11,273,574: Scalable Three Dimensional Printing Apparatus U.S. Patent 10307959B2: Concrete Delivery system [Speaker Notes] Kate
Granted on  march 15 2022 and has over 15 years of protection at a TRL of 6-7
A large scale concrete 3D printer that uses wheels along rails to move the 3D printing trolley. The lengthwise rails are able to be changed to modify the 3D printing area. The design of the printing head allows for use of common concrete. Which distinguishes it from other patents and 3D printer models
Megan Kreiger is the inventor and has demonstrated success with other 3D printers to print functional structures for her intende use case in the army; B-hut (barrack hut) was first design in 2023 using on site materials

