"actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"64731015-0fdb-4f61-871f-90572122317f","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Management Team"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"5320d3e9-d698-4638-863a-c94e3b5e5dfd","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"[Speaker Notes] Kate: sales, leadership, community connections, with flyer enterprise, Presidents Emissary, internships in consultative sales, and going into sales for a staffing firm\nWill: Can be tech expert chief technology officer; I can’t lead r&amp;d but id e decent person to make sure they are on track kinda? Like I can understand it but only the companies have the experience and capability for thedevelopment. So tech oversight works ya\n“Construction attorney with experience in building code compliance and alternative construction methods.”\nOur team is smaller than most here and limited in expertise when it comes to construction and 3D printers so we will need a legal advisor to ensure our structures are up to code and that general contractors trust the structural integrity of our 3D printer’s work. We will also need help with fundraising as costs for creating the first printer is high. We will need a technician to learn the mechanics of the machine to fix when it needs repair. Lastly, we are looking for advice from a homebuilder. We have experience with construction and general engineering, but we do not have a civil engineer or homebuilder who can help us create and validate our work."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.234Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"22083375-b104-4438-8198-3a334b25386f","type":"heading","style":{},"content":{"text":"Project Plan","level":2},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"1183d711-2298-4705-bc18-da36f47a1f9b","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"‹#›"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"bf1ba76e-c523-4959-bfdf-9123af825d4a","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Project Plan"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"091d16f7-121e-4201-95dc-d2bc18887711","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"[Speaker Notes] Equity Investment and TVSF = however much money it takes to build 1 prototype; get half of equity and use that + all of TVSF to have prototype by month 6 and have software developed to program the 3D printer\nBy month 12 have a SBIR to R&amp;D to add tracks and be able to successfully build a demonstration\nSeed equity fund"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T14:39:46.235Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"606d4ba4-d467-47e9-